---
// The "tristan / & other stories" lockup.
//
// Structure (see theme/stories-heading for the mechanics):
//   .sh__wordmark — the full-width "tristan" SVG; fills gutter-to-gutter. JS
//                   measures the glyph bbox and sets the viewBox so width:100%
//                   fills exactly at any viewport (no hardcoded aspect ratio).
//   .sh__amp      — the big "&", overlapping the wordmark (indented). It
//                   parallaxes + fades on its OWN viewport position.
//   .sh__track    — reserves the pin duration in normal flow for "other stories".
//     .sh__pin    — position:sticky at --sh-top; "other stories" pins here.
//       .sh__heading — the outline→solid font-swap reveal that wipes while pinned.
//     .sh__sub    — the page-authored intro, a STATIC SIBLING of the pin (not a
//                   child of it) so it scrolls with the page under its own steam.
//
// The "&" and "other stories" are DECOUPLED: each has its own scroll driver.
//
// This component owns ONLY the lockup. The body copy + video carousel are the
// page's responsibility: they live in the content region that FLOWS BELOW this
// (see FullHeroLayout's .fh__content riser), which rises into the empty space the
// pinned lockup reserves and pushes it away.
//
// "other stories" renders TWICE — an outline layer and a solid layer in the same
// box — so the reveal clip can wipe one over the other.
---

<stories-heading>
	<h1 class="sh__wordmark">
		<svg
			class="sh__wordmark-svg"
			role="img"
			aria-label="tristan"
			viewBox="0 0 1000 300"
			preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMid meet"
		>
			<text x="0" y="240" class="sh__wordmark-text">tristan</text>
		</svg>
	</h1>

	<div class="sh__amp" data-sh-amp aria-hidden="true">&amp;</div>

	<div class="sh__track" data-sh-track>
		<div class="sh__pin" data-sh-pin>
			<h2 class="sh__heading">
				<span class="sh__outline" aria-hidden="true">other stories</span>
				<span class="sh__solid"><wobble-text scale="5" speed="0.3">other stories</wobble-text></span>
			</h2>
		</div>
		{/* Sub-lockup (the page-authored intro). A STATIC SIBLING OF THE PIN, and the
		     sibling part is the whole point: it flows directly below the pin's NATURAL
		     position — which is the top of the track, i.e. exactly under "other stories"
		     at rest — but, not being sticky itself, it then scrolls away with the page
		     under the browser's own compositor.
		     It used to live INSIDE the pin (absolute, top:100%), which glued it to the
		     viewport and forced JS to fake normal scrolling by writing
		     translateY(-scrollY) every frame. That transform is main-thread work racing
		     a compositor-thread scroll, so on touch devices it was permanently a few
		     frames behind the page — the "laggy intro". Nothing can make that smooth;
		     the fix is to not do it. Keep this OUT of the pin.
		     The track has an explicit height, so this reserves no extra flow space —
		     it overlays the empty region the rising body copy fills, exactly as before. */}
		<div class="sh__sub"><slot /></div>
	</div>
</stories-heading>
